ed or updated in the last 7 days OR 200+ stars and new to us\n- Genuinely relevant: agent orchestration, local inference, multi-agent, AI security/DLP, memory/context, OpenClaw-adjacent\n- NOT: tutorials, course repos, awesome-lists, toy projects, or already in the seen list\n\nLoad seen list from /home/jlwestsr/.openclaw/workspace/memory/github-scout-seen.json — skip anything already there.\nPick MAX 3 repos per day. If nothing genuinely interesting, skip fork/research and say so.\n\n## Step 3: Fork + Clone + Research (for each pick)\nFor each selected repo:\n1. Fork to moto-westai: source /home/jlwestsr/.openclaw/secrets/github-moto.env && GITHUB_TOKEN=$GITHUB_MOTO_PAT gh repo fork OWNER/REPO --clone=false\n2. Clone to research-temp: GIT_SSH_COMMAND=\"ssh -i /home/jlwestsr/.ssh/id_ed25519_moto\" git clone git@github.com:moto-westai/REPO.git /home/jlwestsr/projects/research-temp/REPO\n3. Add upstream: cd /home/jlwestsr/projects/research-temp/REPO && git remote add upstream https://github.com/OWNER/REPO.git\n4. Explore: read README, scan directory structure, read key source files (types, core interfaces, main entry point)\n5. Write research note to /home/jlwestsr/.openclaw/workspace/west_ai_labs/docs/research/REPO-scout-YYYY-MM-DD.md — what it does, architecture highlights, relevance to West AI Labs, recommended next steps\n\n## Step 4: Update Seen List\nAdd all researched repos to /home/jlwestsr/.openclaw/workspace/memory/github-scout-seen.json\n\n## Step 5: Deliver Your Report\nYour output IS the delivery — the cron system will automatically send it to Jason via Discord DM. Do NOT use the message tool.\n- Repos found today: name, stars, one-liner\n- Fork + research done per repo\n- Link to research notes written\n- Disk usage of /home/jlwestsr/projects/research-temp/ so Jason can track accumulation\n\nConcise. Daily briefing, not a thesis. If research-temp is getting large, note it and flag for cleanup.",
